{'name': 'debug_parser_output', 'id': 'toolu_01Qom1mkmBidb7W1UxRhmgJu', 'arguments': '{"parser_code": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\"\\"\\"\\nLN6280P Parser - Loan Billing Statement (Enhanced for Multiple Bank Formats)\\n\\nThis parser is designed to handle LN6280P documents from multiple banks including\\nJack Henry (JH) and RegionalBank formats. It uses additive enhancement to support\\nformat variations while maintaining compatibility with the original JH format.\\n\\nENHANCED FEATURES:\\n- Supports both JH and RegionalBank date field labels\\n- Handles customer name prefixes \'3\' (JH) and \'4\' (RegionalBank)  \\n- Extracts phone numbers when present\\n- Supports varied field labels in summary tables\\n- Maintains backward compatibility with original JH format\\n\\nDOCUMENT STRUCTURE:\\nThe LN6280P document typically contains:\\n1. Document header with LN6280P identifier\\n2. Multiple loan billing statements in batch format\\n3. Each statement contains:\\n   - Account header with \'001\' marker and \\"Loan Billing Statement\\" title\\n   - Statement/billing date and account number\\n   - Customer name (prefixed with \'3\' or \'4\') and address lines (prefixed with \'1\')\\n   - Account Activity Summary table with financial details\\n   - Explanation of Amount Due section\\n   - Loan Transaction History table\\n   - Payment stub section (prefixed with \'046\')\\n\\nFORMAT VARIATIONS SUPPORTED:\\n- JH Format: \\"Statement Date\\", \\"Payment Due Date\\", \\"Total Amount Due\\", prefix \'3\'\\n- RegionalBank: \\"Billing Date\\", \\"Due Date\\", \\"Payment Amount Due\\", prefix \'4\', phone numbers\\n\\"\\"\\"\\n\\nimport sys\\nimport json\\nimport re\\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Optional, Tuple\\n\\ndef find_section_boundaries(lines: List[str]) -> List[int]:\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    Finds the starting line index of each new notice section. For LN6280P,\\n    the most reliable marker is the page start marker \'001\' often followed\\n    by the \\"Loan Billing Statement\\" title.\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    boundaries = []\\n    \\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\\n        if line.strip().startswith(\'001\'):\\n            for j in range(i, min(i + 3, len(lines))):\\n                if \\"Loan Billing Statement\\" in lines[j]:\\n                    if i not in boundaries:\\n                        boundaries.append(i)\\n                    break\\n    return boundaries\\n\\ndef extract_document_date(lines: List[str]) -> Optional[str]:\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    Extracts the main document date from the first notice.\\n    ENHANCED: Supports both \\"Statement Date\\" (JH) and \\"Billing Date\\" (RegionalBank)\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    for line in lines:\\n        # Try JH format first\\n        match = re.search(r\'Statement Date\\\\s+(\\\\d{1,2}/\\\\d{1,2}/\\\\d{2})\', line, re.IGNORECASE)\\n        if match:\\n            return match.group(1).strip()\\n        \\n        # Try RegionalBank format\\n        match = re.search(r\'Billing Date\\\\s+(\\\\d{1,2}/\\\\d{1,2}/\\\\d{2})\', line, re.IGNORECASE)\\n        if match:\\n            return match.group(1).strip()\\n    return None\\n\\ndef extract_phone_number(lines: List[str]) -> Optional[str]:\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    Extracts phone number from document if present (RegionalBank format).\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    for line in lines:\\n        match = re.search(r\'Phone Number\\\\s+(\\\\([0-9]{3}\\\\)\\\\s*[0-9]{3}-[0-9]{4})\', line, re.IGNORECASE)\\n        if match:\\n            return match.group(1).strip()\\n    return None\\n\\ndef find_customer_info(lines: List[str]) -> Tuple[Optional[str], List[str]]:\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    Finds customer name and address block using robust patterns.\\n    ENHANCED: Supports both prefix \'3\' (JH) and prefix \'4\' (RegionalBank)\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\\n        stripped = line.strip()\\n        # Try both prefixes - \'3\' for JH, \'4\' for RegionalBank\\n        if stripped.startswith(\'3\') or stripped.startswith(\'4\'):\